AArch64 grant-payload-publish-aarch64-RELAXED-control
(*
 * THE CONTROL THAT GIVES THIS WHOLE TIER ITS REASON TO EXIST.
 *
 * Identical to `grant-payload-publish-aarch64.litmus` with the release/acquire
 * pair DOWNGRADED to plain STR/LDR -- i.e. the same protocol written by someone
 * who thought the memory orders were decoration.
 *
 * RESULT (herd7 7.58, 2026-08-17): **ALLOWED / "Sometimes"** on ARMv8.
 *
 * Read it against `grant-payload-publish-x86-RELAXED-control.litmus`, which is
 * the SAME relaxed code and is **FORBIDDEN** on x86-TSO. That pair is the
 * "passes on x86 for months, faults on ARM64 under a rare schedule" trap, stated
 * as two herd7 verdicts instead of as a warning: relaxing these orders is
 * UNDETECTABLE by any amount of x86 testing and unsound on the architecture this
 * library actually ships on.
 *)
{
0:X0=value; 0:X1=payload;
1:X0=value; 1:X1=payload;
}
 P0             | P1            ;
 MOV W2,#42     | LDR W2,[X0]   ;
 STR W2,[X1]    | LDR W3,[X1]   ;
 MOV W3,#1      |               ;
 STR W3,[X0]    |               ;
exists (1:X2=1 /\ 1:X3=0)
